    "These are warmed, steady camera updates on this Mac at DPR 1; neither physical-iPhone performance nor initial-loading speed is measured.",
    "One-pixel readback forces completion and adds overhead. These are completed update/draw costs, not isolated GPU timer-query terrain timings.",
    "PeakFinder uses its complete public panorama panel, including residual compass/credit UI. Peak labels are hidden. Coelum is tested both as a terrain pass and as skyScene composition; UI event handling and new astronomy-frame computation are excluded.",
    "Elevation sources, native detail, geometry density, projection and shading differ. Matching location, requested range and angular framing does not make the geometric workloads equal.",
    "The portrait FOV convention was calibrated before the final portrait rerun. The earlier mismatched portrait run was excluded from this report.",
    "Request-to-next-completed-frame latency does not prove that a buffered third-party renderer has presented the latest camera command. The conclusion uses completed draw costs and the sustained update cadence.",
    "All tested cases kept up with the 60 Hz requestAnimationFrame loop. Fractions of a millisecond should not be treated as a universal ranking."
